{
  "id": "COMPOUND:20046 - PROTEIN:4996",
  "verbalization": "Phytolaccoside B appears to exert its biological effects through a mechanism involving the inhibition of serine/threonine-protein kinases, specifically ULK2, ULK3, and MARK1. These kinases are central to cellular processes such as autophagy and proliferation, and their inhibition is associated with the suppression of tumor growth. The evidence suggests that Phytolaccoside B targets these kinases, which in turn are involved in the regulation of the NCI-H157 cell line, potentially through a pathway that involves the (1S,2S,5R,6R,7S,8S,11S)-7-hydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-11-[(2R)-1-hydroxypropan-2-yl]-6-methyl-9-oxatricyclo[6.2.1.02,6]undecan-10-one compound. This compound is a known target of the kinases and is implicated in the pathogenesis of the NCI-H157 cells. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust and reliable relationship, supported by the shared mechanism of kinase inhibition. The evidence suggests that Phytolaccoside B may act as a potential therapeutic agent against NCI-H157, particularly through the modulation of these kinases and their downstream effects.",
